Scope

This LICENSE applies only to Glitch Boy project-owned files and additions that
do not already carry a different upstream copyright and license notice. Those
files can be used under the terms above on their own.

The firmware as a whole

This repository is a mixed-license codebase, and the firmware image built from
it combines all of these licenses in one binary:

  - Glitch Boy files and the esp_8_bit foundation: ISC-style (permissive)
  - Walnut-CGB, minigb_apu, and the Parallax font data: MIT
  - Nofrendo: GNU Library General Public License, version 2
  - the music visualizer (midi_visualizer.cpp, vidpix_data.h,
    vidpix_vector_font.h): GNU General Public License, version 3 or later,
    ported from VID PIX PAL v1.2.2 by Synthrotek Sound Study Modular

Because GPL-3.0-or-later code is compiled into the same image, the firmware as
a whole, in source or binary form, is distributed under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or (at your option) any later version. The full text is in
licenses/GPL-3.0.txt. If you redistribute the firmware, you must make the
complete corresponding source available under that license, keep every
copyright and license notice, and pass the same rights on to the recipient.

This does not relicense any individual file. Each file keeps the license in its
own header, and the permissive files above can still be taken out and used
under their own terms. Nofrendo stays under the LGPL v2 for its own files; it
is combined into the GPLv3 firmware as section 6 of that license allows, so the
LGPL v2 obligations (source, relinking materials) still apply to it. See
SOURCE_AND_RELINKING_OFFER.md.

The Game Boy and Game Boy Color implementation under
firmware/GlitchBoy/src/walnut/ includes Walnut-CGB, its Peanut-GB foundation,
marked SameBoy-derived portions, and minigb_apu/MiniGBS audio code. Those
components retain their MIT terms and upstream copyright notices; they are not
relicensed by this file. See the README in that directory and the bundled
license texts under licenses/.

See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the full list of components, and
COMMERCIAL_DISTRIBUTION_NOTES.md for what to include when shipping the firmware
on devices.
